1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,400
TC EMPLOYEE: Hi. Can I help you?

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:09,100
VISITOR: I'd like to find out if you have any excursions suitable for families.

3
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:12,985
TC EMPLOYEE: Sure. How about taking your family for a cruise?

4
00:00:12,985 --> 00:00:16,800
We have a steamship that takes passengers out several times a day

5
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:18,990
it's over 100 years old.

6
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:22,790
VISITOR: That sounds interesting. How long is the trip?

7
00:00:22,790 --> 00:00:24,640
TC EMPLOYEE: About an hour and a half

8
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:27,561
And don't forget to take pictures of the mountains.

9
00:00:27,561 --> 00:00:31,210
They're all around you when you're on the boat and they look fantastic.

10
00:00:31,210 --> 00:00:36,260
VISITOR: OK. And I assume there's a cafe or something on board?

11
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:39,140
TC EMPLOYEE: Sure. How old are your children?

12
00:00:39,140 --> 00:00:43,210
VISITOR: Er, my daughter's fifteen and my son's seven.

13
00:00:43,210 --> 00:00:47,883
TC EMPLOYEE: Right. Well there are various things you can do once you've crossed the lake,

14
00:00:47,883 --> 00:00:53,139
to make a day of it. One thing that's very popular is a visit to the Country Farm.

15
00:00:53,139 --> 00:00:57,812
You're met off the boat by the farmer and he'll take you to the holding pens,

16
00:00:57,812 --> 00:01:00,440
where the sheep are kept. Children love feeding them!

17
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:04,620
VISITOR: My son would love that. He really likes animals.

18
00:01:04,620 --> 00:01:09,670
TC EMPLOYEE: Well, there's also a 40-minute trek round the farm on a horse, if he wants.

19
00:01:09,670 --> 00:01:14,540
VISITOR: Do you think he'd manage it? He hasn't done that before.

20
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:18,310
TC EMPLOYEE: Sure. It's suitable for complete beginners.

21
00:01:18,310 --> 00:01:19,660
VISITOR: Ah, good.

22
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:23,662
TC EMPLOYEE: And again, visitors are welcome to explore the farm on their own,

23
00:01:23,662 --> 00:01:27,092
as long as they take care to close gates and so on.

24
00:01:27,092 --> 00:01:30,320
There are some very beautiful gardens along the side of the lake

25
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:32,237
which also belong to the farm -

26
00:01:32,237 --> 00:01:34,238
they'll be just at their best now.

27
00:01:34,238 --> 00:01:36,810
You could easily spend an hour or two there.

28
00:01:36,810 --> 00:01:42,660
VISITOR: OK. Well that all sounds good. And can we get lunch there?

29
00:01:42,660 --> 00:01:45,100
TC EMPLOYEE: You can, and it's very good

30
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:47,504
though it's not included in the basic cost.

31
00:01:47,504 --> 00:01:49,320
You pay when you get there.

32
00:01:49,320 --> 00:01:50,610
VISITOR: Right.

33
00:01:50,610 --> 00:01:54,740
VISITOR: So is there anything else to do over on that side of the lake?

34
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:58,160
TC EMPLOYEE: Well, what you can do is take a bike over on the ship

35
00:01:58,160 --> 00:02:01,513
and then go on a cycling trip.

36
00:02:01,513 --> 00:02:02,640
There's a trail there called the Back Road

37
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:08,286
you could easily spend three or four hours exploring it, and the scenery's wonderful.

38
00:02:08,286 --> 00:02:09,780
They'll give you a map

39
00:02:09,780 --> 00:02:13,520
when you get your ticket for the cruise - there's no extra charge.

40
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:17,380
VISITOR: What's the trail like in terms of difficulty?

41
00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:19,575
TC EMPLOYEE: Quite challenging in places.

42
00:02:19,575 --> 00:02:25,430
It wouldn't be suitable for your seven-year-old. It needs someone who's got a bit more experience.

43
00:02:25,430 --> 00:02:29,848
VISITOR: Hmm. Well, my daughter loves cycling and so do I,

44
00:02:29,848 --> 00:02:37,078
so maybe the two of us could go, and my wife and son could stay on the farm.

45
00:02:37,078 --> 00:02:40,780
That might work out quite well. But we don't have bikes here

46
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:44,710
is there somewhere we could rent them?

47
00:02:44,710 --> 00:02:50,160
TC EMPLOYEE: Yes, there's a place here in the city. It's called Ratchesons.

48
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:54,160
VISITOR: I'll just make a note of that - er, how do you spell it?

49
00:02:54,160 --> 00:03:04,010
TC EMPLOYEE: R-A-T-C-H-E-S-O-N-S. It's just by the cruise ship terminal.

50
00:03:04,010 --> 00:03:05,660
VISITOR: OK.

51
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:11,212
TC EMPLOYEE: You'd also need to pick up a repair kit for the bike from there to take along with you,

52
00:03:11,212 --> 00:03:13,520
and you'd need to take along a snack and some water

53
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:16,500
it'd be best to get those in the city.

54
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:18,920
VISITOR: Fine. That shouldn't be a problem

55
00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:23,260
And I assume I can rent a helmet from the bike place?

56
00:03:23,260 --> 00:03:25,622
TC EMPLOYEE: Sure, you should definitely get that.

57
00:03:25,622 --> 00:03:30,050
It's a great ride, but you want to be well prepared because it's very remote -

58
00:03:30,050 --> 00:03:33,620
you won't see any shops round there, or anywhere to stay

59
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:36,840
so you need to get back in time for the last boat.

60
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:41,580
VISITOR: Yeah. So what sort of prices are we looking at here?

61
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:44,500
TC EMPLOYEE: Let's see, that'd be one adult

62
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:48,720
and one child for the cruise with farm tour,

63
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:53,220
that's $117, and an adult and a child for the cruise only

64
00:03:53,220 --> 00:03:55,860
so that's $214 dollars altogether.

65
00:03:55,860 --> 00:04:00,900
Oh, wait a minute, how old did you say your daughter was?

66
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:02,590
VISITOR: Fifteen.

67
00:04:02,590 --> 00:04:09,014
TC EMPLOYEE: Then I'm afraid it's $267 because she has to pay the adult fare,

68
00:04:09,014 --> 00:04:15,010
which is $75 instead of the child fare which is $22 - sorry about that.

69
00:04:15,010 --> 00:04:18,270
VISITOR: That's OK. Er, so how do...
